        "kind": "loop_objective",
        "canonical_id": "repeat-until-limit.objective",
        "statement": "A backward-branching loop must always terminate: it exits forward when its condition is true, and when the charged iterations would exceed max_iterations it traps rather than exiting or looping forever.",
        "observable_success_condition": "For every execution, the VM either reaches exit_next within max_iterations charged iterations, or traps; it never loops unbounded and never exits without the condition being observed true.",
